[2] (function_call) {'type': 'function_call', 'name': 'write_file', 'arguments': '{"file_path":"/project/outputs/scripts/finalize_fig2b.py","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nimport shutil, json\\nOUT=Path(\'project/outputs\')\\nFIG=OUT/\'figures\'; TAB=OUT/\'tables\'; REP=OUT/\'reports\'\\naccepted=5\\ncopies={\\n    FIG/f\'fig2b_spatial_scatter_attempt{accepted}.png\': FIG/\'fig2b_spatial_scatter.png\',\\n    FIG/f\'fig2b_spatial_scatter_attempt{accepted}.pdf\': FIG/\'fig2b_spatial_scatter.pdf\',\\n    TAB/f\'fig2b_spatial_scatter_plot_data_attempt{accepted}.csv\': TAB/\'fig2b_spatial_scatter_plot_data.csv\',\\n    TAB/f\'compare_metrics_attempt{accepted}.json\': TAB/\'compare_metrics.json\',\\n    FIG/f\'compare_figures_attempt{accepted}.png\': FIG/\'compare_diff.png\',\\n}\\nfor src,dst in copies.items():\\n    if not src.exists(): raise FileNotFoundError(src)\\n    shutil.copyfile(src,dst)\\n    print(f\'copied {src} -> {dst}\')\\n# Build concise note with metric trajectory.\\nmetrics=[]\\nfor i in range(1,accepted+1):\\n    p=TAB/f\'compare_metrics_attempt{i}.json\'\\n    if p.exists():\\n        d=json.loads(p.read_text())\\n        metrics.append({\\n            \'attempt\': i,\\n            \'phash_hamming\': d.get(\'phash_hamming\'),\\n            \'ssim\': d.get(\'ssim\'),\\n            \'orb_good_matches\': d.get(\'orb_good_matches\'),\\n            \'palette_mean_delta_e\': d.get(\'palette_mean_delta_e\'),\\n            \'text_match_rate\': d.get(\'text_diff\',{}).get(\'match_rate\'),\\n            \'b_level_prior\': d.get(\'b_level_prior\'),\\n            \'geometry_clean\': d.get(\'pass2_geometry\',{}).get(\'clean\'),\\n            \'geometry_findings\': d.get(\'pass2_geometry\',{}).get(\'findings\'),\\n        })\\nfinal=metrics[-1]\\nnote=f\\"\\"\\"# Fig. 2b spatial scatterplot reproduction note\\n\\n## Inputs\\n\\n- Dataset: `library/datasets/dataset_lohoff_et_al_seqfish.h5ad`\\n- Target image: `project/uploads/Fig2b.jpg` (592 × 784 px)\\n\\n## Data fields and subset\\n\\n- AnnData shape: 19,416 cells × 351 genes.\\n- Spatial coordinates: `adata.obsm[\'spatial\']`, plotted as `x` and `y`.\\n- Cell type field: `adata.obs[\'celltype_mapped_refined\']`.\\n- The y-axis was inverted using the plotting-axis inversion (`ax.invert_yaxis()`), matching the image-coordinate orientation of the reference.\\n- Cells labelled `Low quality` (1,645 cells) were excluded from the reproduced panel because the reference legend has no corresponding class and the target panel distinguishes annotated tissue cell types. The final plotted-data table therefore contains 17,771 cells.\\n\\n## Palette and category reconciliation\\n\\n- Palette source tier: tier 3, swatches measured from the reference legend by `project/skills/figure-reproduce/scripts/build_colormap.py` using the explicit legend box `295,20,585,725`.\\n- Colormap verification: `build_colormap.py --verify project/outputs/tables/colormap.yaml` returned provenance OK.\\n- All plotted categories are covered by `tables/colormap.yaml`.\\n- Dataset category naming differs from the target for `Haematoendothelial progenitors`; the legend label in the reproduction uses the target spelling `Hematoendothelial progenitors`, while the plotted cells retain the dataset category in the CSV.\\n- Reference-only legend entries shown in `Fig2b.jpg` but absent from this AnnData object were retained in the legend for visual fidelity: `Blood progenitors`, `Caudal mesoderm`, and `ExE endoderm`. Their colors were measured from the target swatches; no points are plotted for those classes.\\n- Dataset-only category `Low quality` was not plotted and is not in `colormap.yaml`; this is recorded as a deviation from plotting all AnnData observations.\\n\\n## Rendering parameters\\n\\n- Canvas: 592 × 784 px, white background, no axes/ticks.\\n- Scatter marker: circular, area 3.0 pt², opaque, no outline, rasterized in the PDF.\\n- Scatter axes box: left/bottom/width/height = `0.030,0.542,0.441,0.435` in figure fraction.\\n- Annotations: panel label `b`, a visual `250 µm` scale bar, and the A/D/V/P orientation compass were added to match the provided target crop. The source coordinates are normalized, so the scale bar is a reference-layout annotation rather than a recalibrated physical measurement from the h5ad file.\\n- Legend: target order and target label text, Arial 12 pt, label spacing 0.82, anchor `(0.505, 0.960)`.\\n\\n## Attempt trajectory\\n\\n| Attempt | pHash Hamming ↓ | SSIM ↑ | ORB matches ↑ | Palette mean dE ↓ | Text match rate ↑ | B-level prior | Geometry clean |\\n|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|:---:|:---:|\\n\\"\\"\\"\\nfor m in metrics:\\n    note += f\\"| {m[\'attempt\']} | {m[\'phash_hamming\']} | {m[\'ssim\']} | {m[\'orb_good_matches\']} | {m[\'palette_mean_delta_e\']} | {m[\'text_match_rate\']} | {m[\'b_level_prior\']} | {m[\'geometry_clean\']} |\\\\n\\"\\nnote += f\\"\\"\\"\\n\\nAccepted attempt: {accepted}.\\n\\nFinal comparison files:\\n\\n- Metrics JSON: `project/outputs/tables/compare_metrics.json`\\n- Visual target/reproduction/overlay diff: `project/outputs/figures/compare_diff.png`\\n\\n## Verification result and residual differences\\n\\n- The final canvas dimensions and aspect ratio match the target exactly (592 × 784 px; aspect 0.7551).\\n- Automated orientation check selected `as_is`; vertical/horizontal flips scored worse, consistent with the requested inverted y-axis.\\n- Final metrics improved over attempt 1: pHash Hamming 12 → {final[\'phash_hamming\']}, SSIM 0.5891 → {final[\'ssim\']}, and ORB matches 156 → {final[\'orb_good_matches\']}.\\n- The comparison script still reports a palette dE warning. This was not repaired by further rendering because the plotted category colors are already taken from the measured reference legend. The residual warning is driven by comparing dominant anti-aliased/JPEG panel colors rather than label-bound swatches; `extract_reference_spec.py` also marked whole-panel palette recovery as LOW reliability for this dense compressed scatter.\\n- The provided target crop contains partial grey/pink neighboring-panel content at the lower-left outside the requested spatial scatterplot. This was not reproduced because it is not supported as part of the requested panel in the supplied AnnData data.\\n- Minor remaining differences include JPEG/anti-aliasing texture, exact font metrics, and categories present in the reference legend but absent from the dataset (`Blood progenitors`, `Caudal mesoderm`, `ExE endoderm`).\\n\\n## Output artifacts\\n\\n- `project/outputs/figures/fig2b_spatial_scatter.png`\\n- `project/outputs/figures/fig2b_spatial_scatter.pdf`\\n- `project/outputs/tables/fig2b_spatial_scatter_plot_data.csv`\\n- `project/outputs/tables/colormap.yaml`\\n- `project/outputs/tables/compare_metrics.json`\\n- `project/outputs/figures/compare_diff.png`\\n\\"\\"\\"\\n(REP/\'fig2b_spatial_scatter_repro_note.md\').write_text(note)\\nprint(f\'wrote {REP/\\"fig2b_spatial_scatter_repro_note.md\\"}\')\\n\\nrequired=[FIG/\'fig2b_spatial_scatter.png\', FIG/\'fig2b_spatial_scatter.pdf\', TAB/\'fig2b_spatial_scatter_plot_data.csv\', TAB/\'colormap.yaml\', TAB/\'compare_metrics.json\', FIG/\'compare_diff.png\', REP/\'fig2b_spatial_scatter_repro_note.md\']\\nmissing=[str(p) for p in required if not p.exists()]\\nif missing:\\n    raise SystemExit(\'missing required artifacts: \'+\', \'.join(missing))\\nprint(\'all required final artifacts exist\')\\n"}', 'call_id': 'call_oBMpNNZ6IT7jTXdlH9ZSBEQE', 'id': 'fc_024bb976f67ed26d006aa44b3f9c0887d2aa6dcae642cdb0d1', 'index': 1}
