- Recreated the Fig. 2b-style spatial cell-type scatterplot from `library/datasets/dataset_lohoff_et_al_seqfish.h5ad`.
- Used `obsm["spatial"]` for cell positions and `obs["celltype_mapped_refined"]` for cell type colors.
- Inverted the y-axis to match the reference image orientation.
- Final accepted render was attempt 5.
- Final comparison improved over attempt 1:
  - pHash Hamming: 12 → 6
  - SSIM: 0.5891 → 0.7188
  - ORB matches: 156 → 186

Decisions & assumptions:
- Palette was measured from the reference legend using the figure-reproduction workflow; `colormap.yaml` provenance verified successfully.
- `Low quality` cells were excluded because the reference legend has no corresponding class.
- Reference-only legend entries absent from the AnnData object — `Blood progenitors`, `Caudal mesoderm`, and `ExE endoderm` — were retained in the legend for visual fidelity, but no points were plotted for them.
- Added the panel label, scale bar, and A/D/V/P compass to match the provided reference crop.
- The comparison script still flags a palette dE warning, but the plotted colors are from the measured reference legend; this residual is documented as likely due to dense JPEG/anti-aliased scatter color blending.
- The target crop includes partial lower-left neighboring-panel content that was not reproduced because it is not part of the requested spatial scatterplot and is unsupported by the supplied AnnData.

